# Reusable controls and presentation data. Rendering lives in ui_native.dl.
import lib/ui.dl

a UI component {integer:kind} labeled {C string:text} styled {C string:variant} at {integer:left} {integer:top} sized {integer:width} by {integer:height} containing {an array:children} means: UI node kind with text colored "" sized 0 by 0 bordered 0 containing children acting no UI action at left top measuring width by height styled variant
a UI text component {integer:kind} labeled {C string:text} styled {C string:variant} means: a UI component kind labeled text styled variant at 0 0 sized 0 by 0 containing no UI children

eyebrow {C string:text} means: a UI text component 13 labeled text styled ""
title {C string:text} means: a UI text component 14 labeled text styled ""
accent title {C string:text} means: a UI text component 14 labeled text styled "accent"
heading {C string:text} means: a UI text component 24 labeled text styled ""
brand {C string:text} means: a UI text component 24 labeled text styled "brand"
caption {C string:text} means: a UI text component 15 labeled text styled ""
badge {C string:text} means: a UI text component 27 labeled text styled ""
space of {integer:height} pixels means: a UI component 16 labeled "" styled "" at 0 0 sized 0 by height containing no UI children
primary button {C string:text} means: a UI text component 2 labeled text styled "primary"
quiet button {C string:text} means: a UI text component 2 labeled text styled "quiet"
switch {C string:text} means: a UI text component 17 labeled text styled ""
option {C string:text} means: a UI text component 19 labeled text styled ""
statistic {C string:text} means: a UI text component 21 labeled text styled ""

section panel at {integer:left} {integer:top} sized {integer:width} by {integer:height}:
    result: UI reference
    body:
        children: many UI reference
    value:
        a UI component 12 labeled "" styled "card" at left top sized width by height containing (the body's children)

section group at {integer:left} {integer:top} sized {integer:width} by {integer:height}:
    result: UI reference
    body:
        children: many UI reference
    value:
        a UI component 12 labeled "" styled "plain" at left top sized width by height containing (the body's children)

section page {C string:name}:
    result: UI reference
    body:
        children: many UI reference
    value:
        a UI container of kind 22 containing (the body's children) named name

a UI container of kind {integer:kind} containing {an array:children} named {C string:name} means: a UI component kind labeled name styled "" at 0 0 sized 0 by 0 containing children

section choices {C string:name}:
    result: UI reference
    body:
        children: many UI reference
    value:
        a UI component 18 labeled name styled "" at 0 0 sized 0 by 0 containing (the body's children)

canvas {C string:name} at {integer:left} {integer:top} sized {integer:width} by {integer:height} means: a UI component 20 labeled name styled "" at left top sized width by height containing no UI children
the interface uses [a|an] {C string:name} theme means: a UI text component 25 labeled name styled ""
the interface fits {integer:width} by {integer:height} pixels means: a UI component 26 labeled "" styled "" at 0 0 sized width by height containing no UI children

to get the UI element labeled {C string:label} in {UI reference:root}:
    if root's text = label:
        return root
    set index to 0
    loop while index < root's count:
        set found to the UI element labeled label in (the UI child at index in root)
        if found != @intrinsic("construct", UI reference):
            return found
        increment index
    return @intrinsic("construct", UI reference)

to get the control labeled {C string:label} in {a pointer to UI instance:instance}:
    set found to the UI element labeled label in (instance's description)
    require condition (found != @intrinsic("construct", UI reference)) reporting "The UI control does not exist"
    return found

to get the position of UI option {string:text} in {UI reference:node}:
    set index to 0
    loop while (index < node's count) and ((the UI child at index in node)'s text != text):
        increment index
    require condition (index < node's count) reporting "The tool field value must match one of its options"
    return index

to select UI option {integer:index} from {UI reference:node} into {a pointer to UI value:value}:
    set chosen to the UI child at index in node
    set value's number to index
    set value's text to chosen's text

to get the UI value for {UI reference:node} in {a pointer to UI instance:instance}:
    set entry to instance's values
    loop while entry != @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI value):
        if entry's target = node:
            return entry
        set entry to entry's next
    set {new entry} to a new UI value
    set new entry's target to node
    set new entry's text to node's text
    if node's kind = 34:
        set index to the position of UI option (the string form of (node's text)) in node
        select UI option index from node into (the address of new entry)
    if node's kind = 21:
        set new entry's text to "0"
    set new entry's next to instance's values
    set instance's values to storage for one slot initialized with new entry
    return instance's values

to set the text of {C string:label} in {a pointer to UI instance:instance} to {a value:text}:
    set node to the control labeled label in instance
    set entry to the UI value for node in instance
    if node's kind = 34:
        select UI option (the position of UI option (the string form of text) in node) from node into entry
    else:
        set entry's text to the string form of text

to set the value of {C string:label} in {a pointer to UI instance:instance} to {integer:number}:
    set node to the control labeled label in instance
    set entry to the UI value for node in instance
    if node's kind = 34:
        select UI option number from node into entry
    else:
        set entry's number to number

to get the value of {C string:label} in {a pointer to UI instance:instance}:
    return (the UI value for (the control labeled label in instance) in instance)'s number

to get the {C string:label} switch is on in {a pointer to UI instance:instance}:
    return (the value of label in instance) != 0

to show page {C string:name} in {a pointer to UI instance:instance}:
    set instance's page to the control labeled name in instance
    require condition (instance's page's kind = 22) reporting "The selected UI element is not a page"

to bind {UI reference:target} in {a pointer to UI instance:instance} to {a callback:action} for event {integer:event}:
    set handler to @intrinsic("construct", UI handler, target, @intrinsic("cast", action, a pointer), instance's handlers, event)
    set instance's handlers to storage for one slot initialized with handler

section when the {C string:label} control changes:
    receiver: a pointer to UI instance
    returns: nothing
    value:
        bind (the control labeled label in this window) in this window to @intrinsic("deferred body") for event 0

to get the action for {UI reference:target} in {a pointer to UI instance:instance} for event {integer:event}:
    set handler to instance's handlers
    loop while handler != @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI handler):
        if (handler's target = target) and (handler's event = event):
            return handler's action
        set handler to handler's next
    return no UI action

to activate {UI reference:node} belonging to {UI reference:parent} in {a pointer to UI instance:instance}:
    set target to node
    if node's kind = 17:
        set entry to the UI value for node in instance
        set entry's number to 1 - entry's number
    if (node's kind = 19) or (node's kind = 29):
        set target to parent
        set index to 0
        loop while (the UI child at index in parent) != node:
            increment index
        set entry to the UI value for parent in instance
        set entry's number to index
    set action to the action for target in instance for event 0
    if action != no UI action:
        @intrinsic("call pointer", action, nothing, instance)
